<body>

  <header>
    <h1>ScamGaurd</h1>
    <p>The all‑in‑one Discord security bot that automatically removes scam links, suspicious images, and protects your community 24/7.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>What is ScamGaurd?</h2>
    <p>
      ScamGaurd is a powerful Discord moderation and security bot designed to keep servers safe from scams, malicious links, and harmful content.
      When a user sends a suspicious link or an image that violates your rules, ScamGaurd automatically removes the content and issues a warning.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Key Features</h2>
    <div class="features">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🔗 Scam Link Detection</h3>
        <p>Automatically detects and removes suspicious or malicious links before members can fall victim.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🖼️ Image Filtering</h3>
        <p>Removes images when image sharing is not allowed or when content is considered unsafe.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>⚠️ Automatic Warnings</h3>
        <p>Users receive instant warnings when they break rules, helping educate them and prevent repeat offenses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🛡️ Server Protection</h3>
        <p>Designed to reduce scams, phishing attempts, and malicious activity across your Discord server.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <p>
      ScamGaurd continuously monitors messages in your Discord server. When a message is sent:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Messages are scanned for suspicious or known scam links</li>
      <li>Images are checked against your server rules</li>
      <li>Rule‑breaking content is removed automatically</li>
      <li>The user receives a warning explaining what they did wrong</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All of this happens instantly, without moderators needing to step in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Commands (Example)</h2>
    <p>You can customize this section based on your actual bot commands.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>/scamguard status</code> – Check if protection is active</li>
      <li><code>/scamguard warnings</code> – View a user's warnings</li>
      <li><code>/scamguard config</code> – Configure protection settings</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

